  <data name="OnboardingWelcomeText" xml:space="preserve"><value>Nice to have you here. Let’s set up the app quickly.</value></data>
  <data name="OnboardingWelcomeHint" xml:space="preserve"><value>Take a moment on the next few pages – it’s worth reading through them.</value></data>
  <data name="OnboardingWhyTitle" xml:space="preserve"><value>Why this day planner?</value></data>
  <data name="OnboardingWhyTraining" xml:space="preserve"><value>You train your brain to lose the hurdle and negativity towards tasks / duties of life. This happens by planning For You and To Do tasks.</value></data>
  <data name="OnboardingWhyPlan" xml:space="preserve"><value>Plan consciously and benefit from the psychological foundations of</value></data>
  <data name="OnboardingWhyActivation" xml:space="preserve"><value>Behavioral activation</value></data>
  <data name="OnboardingWhySelfDetermination" xml:space="preserve"><value>Self-determination</value></data>
  <data name="OnboardingWhySelfCare" xml:space="preserve"><value>Self-care through a plan</value></data>
  <data name="OnboardingWhyReward" xml:space="preserve"><value>The reward system from learning theory</value></data>
  <data name="OnboardingSceneMinutes" xml:space="preserve"><value>Minutes</value></data>
  <data name="OnboardingSceneQuestion" xml:space="preserve"><value>Do you know the Pomodoro technique?</value></data>
  <data name="OnboardingSceneYes" xml:space="preserve"><value>Yes</value></data>
  <data name="OnboardingSceneNo" xml:space="preserve"><value>No</value></data>
  <data name="OnboardingSceneExplain" xml:space="preserve"><value>The Pomodoro technique: 1. Set a task and focus on only that one task, ideally for 30 minutes. 2. Take a short break (have a drink, take a short walk, stretch, etc.) – without distractions that could affect your next focus session, or that are themselves further subtasks (e.g. cleaning one of five windows, continuing to write your novel). 3. Distractions or spontaneous task ideas are normal: jot them down quickly, or add a new task directly in the app and continue with the one you already started.</value></data>
  <data name="OnboardingSceneTip" xml:space="preserve"><value>Goal: Splitting tasks up and working on them deliberately reduces resistance to big tasks (the typical, overly long and postponed to-do list). It also looks after your mental and physical battery through breaks and a realistic amount of time to work.</value></data>
  <data name="OnboardingSceneTipExample" xml:space="preserve"><value>An example: vacuum the flat for 20 minutes, then take a 5-minute break with a walk outside for some fresh air. A bad break: watching a video or shorts, or carrying on with a hobby project.</value></data>
  <data name="OnboardingSceneDayIntro" xml:space="preserve"><value>This is where your day happens. You see a positive to-do book. It has two areas [ For You ] [ To Do ]. In each of these areas you can create tasks.</value></data>
  <data name="OnboardingSceneScope" xml:space="preserve"><value>You can use this positive to-do book for work and for private life, or set just one area.</value></data>
